 "result": "**September 2026 had the highest order revenue: \u20ac150.00, from 2 orders.**\n\n| Month | Revenue (\u20ac) | Orders |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2026-09 | 150.00 | 2 |\n| 2026-11 | 140.00 | 3 (+1 with no total) |\n| 2026-10 | 89.00 | 1 |\n| 2026-08 | 84.00 | 2 |\n| 2026-07 | 19.00 | 1 |\n\nTwo rows have data problems:\n\n- **Order #4 (USB hub, \u20ac25)** has its date written as `12/10/2026`, unlike the other rows. It can't be 10 December, since that date hasn't happened yet, so it's probably 12 October. That would bring October to \u20ac114, which is still below September.\n- **Order #10 (Keyboard stand, 2026-11-10)** has no total recorded. If that order was worth more than \u20ac10, November would beat September. November is also still in progress.\n\nSo September is the answer based on the data as it stands, but it's only \u20ac10 ahead of November.",
